// @error is a compiler intrinsic and cannot be redefined
// A wide store width is EMITTER-INTERCEPTED now, so a user definition of the name
// is reserved — the same rule the other fourteen lowered memory intrinsics follow.
//
// This cell CHANGED, and the change is the point. While `__store_f64__` had no
// emitter arm, `function __store_f64__(…)` genuinely shadowed the builtin and
// genuinely ran, and that escape hatch was deliberately preserved — the
// declared-but-unlowered diagnostic was gated on `fnDeclIx` not holding the name.
// Acquiring an arm closes the hatch: the call site is rewritten to `f64.store`
// before any declaration is looked up, so this body would never run. VL rejects
// the DEFINITION, where the author can see it, rather than letting the call
// quietly mean something else.
function __store_f64__(a: i32, v: f64) {
  0
}
__store_f64__(0, 1.5)
print(1)
